OL,3,GNEWSACall for government help over
OL,4,A'forever chemicals' site
OL,5,
OL,6,FA council leader has called for
OL,7,Fgovernment intervention over
OL,8,Fcontamination by the toxic chemical
OL,9,FPFOA after blood tests found elevated
OL,10,Flevels in some local residents.
OL,12,FMichael Vincent, the leader of Wyre
OL,13,FCouncil, said the issue in
OL,14,FThornton-Cleveleys, Lancashire, was too
OL,15,Flarge for local authorities and the
OL,16,FEnvironment Agency to handle alone.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
